Subject: [PROPOSED P19 SR1 v2] mfreadwrite: keep seek epochs and sample/callback agreement

Retain GE's >200 ms new-source/replacement normalization and >2 s positive
timestamp-jump correction, including its duration/EOS machinery. An explicit
SetCurrentPosition is not a new movie: preserve that first sample's epoch.
Apply any correction exactly once to both sample and callback timestamps,
including already queued responses and zero-valued timestamps.

Six injected GE-shape controls retain P18's compatibility behavior and fix
its timestamp/seek assertions. This is intentionally narrower than v1:
the separate staggered-native-stream absolute-offset test remains failing.
No claim that GE's initial per-stream normalization is Windows-equivalent.
No SR2 demux change. Proposed only, not in an active candidate series.

